<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Resileos — Own the record. Control the story.</title>
  <meta name="description" content="A machine that keeps exact facts, refuses to invent, and gets more capable as your hubs fill. Stores, derives, and abstains. Studio + free key." />
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#06080e" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css" />
</head>
<body>
  <nav class="nav" aria-label="Primary">
    <div class="nav-inner">
      <a class="logo" href="#top"><span class="logo-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span> Resileos</a>
      <div class="nav-links">
        <a class="hide-sm" href="#sells">What it does</a>
        <a class="hide-sm" href="#studio">Studio</a>
        <a class="hide-sm" href="#hubs">Hubs</a>
        <a class="hide-sm" href="#bench">Proof</a>
        <a class="hide-sm" href="#roadmap">Next</a>
        <a href="#pricing">Pricing</a>
        <a class="nav-cta" href="#start">Get free key</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <header class="hero" id="top">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">Stores · derives · abstains</div>
      <h1>Remembers exactly.<br><span class="line2">Grows with your hub.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A machine that <strong>keeps exact facts</strong>, <strong>refuses to invent</strong>, and gets
        <strong>more capable as hubs fill</strong>. Learn a fact, ask it back, get that fact.
        Ask the unknown — get a clear empty answer. Open <strong>Studio</strong> or call the API. Free key to start.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#start">Get a free key</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#hubs">See hubs grow</a>
      </div>
      <p class="micro">Frontier models approximate and can invent on structured truth. This one stores, derives, and abstains.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="panel" aria-label="What it does">
      <div class="tag">WHAT IT DOES</div>
      <div class="row m"># Remembers exactly</div>
      <div class="row">learn Zeus · domain · sky</div>
      <div class="row k">→ ask “Zeus domain” → sky</div>
      <br />
      <div class="row m"># Does not make things up</div>
      <div class="row">ask “Zeus ssn”</div>
      <div class="row c">→ empty / ABSTAINED</div>
      <br />
      <div class="row m"># Grows with your hub</div>
      <div class="row">user: · world: · org: fill with your facts</div>
      <div class="row k">→ more facts → more you can ask and derive</div>
    </aside>
  </header>

  <div class="strip">
    <div class="strip-inner">
      <div><strong>Remembers exactly</strong> — same fact out that you put in</div>
      <div><strong>Refuses to invent</strong> — unknowns stay empty</div>
      <div><strong>Grows with hubs</strong> — capability scales with what you store</div>
      <div><strong>Studio + API</strong> — learn and ask without a contract</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section id="sells">
    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Keeps exact facts. Refuses to invent. Gets more capable as your hubs fill.
      On structured truth, frontier models approximate and invent — this one stores, derives, and abstains.
    </p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <span class="badge badge-ok">REMEMBERS</span>
        <h3>Exact store</h3>
        <p>Learn a triple. Ask it back. Get that object — the same fact you stored.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="badge badge-ok">ABSTAINS</span>
        <h3>Refuses to invent</h3>
        <p>Unknowns return empty / ABSTAINED / NO_ROWS. Derivations stay tied to what you put in.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="badge badge-ok">GROWS</span>
        <h3>Hubs fill → more capability</h3>
        <p>Every fact in <code>user:</code>, <code>world:</code>, or <code>org:</code> is another answer you can ask for — and another hop you can derive.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="badge badge-ok">STUDIO</span>
        <h3>Learn and ask without code</h3>
        <p>Open Studio, save a fact, ask it back. Same API keys as paid hosting.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="badge badge-ok">START</span>
        <h3>Free key + API</h3>
        <p>No contract to begin. Send <code>X-API-Key</code> on every protected route. Mouth off by default — the store comes first.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="badge badge-ok">HARDWARE</span>
        <h3>float32 on normal hosts</h3>
        <p>Default state width is float32. Ordinary CPU is enough for the record. float64 is opt-in.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt" id="studio">
    <div class="inner">
      <h2>Studio — learn, ask, get the fact or empty</h2>
      <p class="sub">
        For non-technical visitors: open Studio, save a fact, ask it back.
        Developers can use the same routes with curl; Docker and self-host stay in the repo docs, not here.
      </p>
      <div class="studio-mock" aria-label="Studio loop mock from real UI">
        <div class="studio-chrome">
          <div class="studio-dot"></div><div class="studio-dot"></div><div class="studio-dot"></div>
          <span>Resileos Studio · streamlit run ui_studio.py</span>
        </div>
        <div class="studio-body">
          <aside class="studio-side">
            <div class="studio-label">Sidebar</div>
            <div class="studio-field"><span>API key</span><code>••••••••</code></div>
            <div class="studio-field"><span>User id</span><code>anon</code></div>
            <div class="studio-field"><span>Persona</span><code>Honest</code></div>
            <div class="studio-teach">
              <div class="studio-label">Save fact</div>
              <div><code>Zeus</code> · <code>domain</code> · <code>sky</code></div>
              <div class="studio-btn">Save fact</div>
              <div class="studio-btn ghost">Seed demo facts</div>
            </div>
            <div class="studio-metrics">
              <div>API <strong>Ready</strong></div>
              <div>Facts <strong>6+</strong></div>
            </div>
          </aside>
          <div class="studio-main">
            <div class="studio-tabs">
              <span class="on">Chat</span><span>Search</span><span>Media</span><span>Diagnostics</span><span>Help</span>
            </div>
            <div class="studio-chat">
              <div class="bubble asst">Resileos Studio — exact memory. Try <code>Zeus domain</code> or <code>remember Zeus domain sky</code>.</div>
              <div class="bubble user">remember Zeus domain sky</div>
              <div class="bubble asst ok">Saved <strong>Zeus —domain→ sky</strong></div>
              <div class="bubble user">Zeus domain</div>
              <div class="bubble asst ok">sky</div>
              <div class="bubble user">Zeus ssn</div>
              <div class="bubble asst empty">No rows · ABSTAINED — unknown stays empty</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="hint" style="margin-top:14px">
        Mock built from <code>src/resileos/ui/studio_app.py</code> (sidebar Save fact / Seed demo / Chat tabs).
        Seed demo facts match the UI button: Zeus/Poseidon/Athena domains + olympian links.
      </p>

      <div class="grid-2" style="margin-top:28px" id="start">
        <div>
          <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;margin-bottom:12px">Three steps — free</h2>
          <div class="steps">
            <div class="step"><div><h3>Get a free key</h3><p>No card. Key is shown once. Send as <code>X-API-Key</code>.</p></div></div>
            <div class="step"><div><h3>Open Studio or call learn</h3><p>Paste the key. Save a fact (or use Seed demo facts).</p></div></div>
            <div class="step"><div><h3>Ask it back</h3><p>Known → the object. Unknown → empty. That is the product.</p></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-ok">FREE · NO CARD</span>
          <h3>Issue your API key</h3>
          <p style="margin-bottom:12px">Optional email for recovery. Mouth stays off by default.</p>
          <form class="form" id="free-key-form">
            <label for="email">Email (optional)</label>
            <input id="email" name="email" type="email" placeholder="you@lab.dev" autocomplete="email" />
            <label for="name">Label</label>
            <input id="name" name="name" type="text" placeholder="my-laptop" maxlength="64" />
            <button class="btn btn-primary btn-block" type="submit">Get free key</button>
            <div class="msg" id="free-key-msg" aria-live="polite"></div>
          </form>
          <div class="key-reveal" id="key-reveal" role="status"></div>
          <p class="micro" style="margin-top:12px">
            Shared public demo namespace: <span class="pending">COMING SOON</span> —
            seed your own facts (or Studio “Seed demo facts”) today.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="hubs">
    <h2>Hubs fill — capability grows</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Your memory lives under <code>user:</code>, <code>world:</code>, and <code>org:</code>.
      As those basins fill with verified facts, you can ask more — and derive more — without inventing.
    </p>
    <div class="hub-grow" aria-label="Hub growth">
      <div class="hub-stage">
        <div class="hub-label">Day 1</div>
        <div class="hub-bar"><span style="width:18%"></span></div>
        <div class="hub-facts">A few facts · answer what you just learned</div>
      </div>
      <div class="hub-stage">
        <div class="hub-label">As you teach</div>
        <div class="hub-bar"><span style="width:48%"></span></div>
        <div class="hub-facts">Project world: fills · chains across stored relations</div>
      </div>
      <div class="hub-stage active">
        <div class="hub-label">Hubs filled</div>
        <div class="hub-bar"><span style="width:86%"></span></div>
        <div class="hub-facts">user: · world: · org: dense · more asks, still no invention</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
      <div class="card">
        <span class="badge">user:</span>
        <h3><code>user:&lt;id&gt;</code></h3>
        <p>Your personal basin — preferences, notes, what Studio’s User id writes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="badge">world:</span>
        <h3><code>world:&lt;id&gt;</code></h3>
        <p>Shared project memory. Seed example: <code>world:materials</code> status / store / mouth.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="badge">org:</span>
        <h3><code>org:&lt;id&gt;</code></h3>
        <p>Team basin — org facts that stay off the global seed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="codebox" style="margin-top:16px">
      <pre>learn  user:alice  prefers  exact_answers
ask    user:alice  prefers  →  exact_answers

# More hub facts → more you can ask and derive
# Still abstains when the hub has no answer</pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt" id="quickstart">
    <div class="inner">
      <h2>API quickstart (same store Studio uses)</h2>
      <p class="sub">For builders. Visitors can skip this and stay in Studio. Header: <code>X-API-Key</code>.</p>
      <div class="tabs" role="tablist">
        <button class="tab active" data-tab="learn" type="button">1 · Learn</button>
        <button class="tab" data-tab="query" type="button">2 · Query</button>
        <button class="tab" data-tab="chain" type="button">3 · Chain</button>
      </div>
      <div class="codebox" data-panel="learn">
        <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="learn">Copy</button>
        <pre id="code-learn">export BASE="https://api.yourdomain.dev/api/v1"
export KEY="rsk_…"

curl -sS -X POST "$BASE/learn" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-API-Key: $KEY" \
  -d '{"subject":"Zeus","relation":"domain","obj":"sky"}'</pre>
      </div>
      <div class="codebox" data-panel="query" hidden>
        <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="query">Copy</button>
        <pre id="code-query">curl -sS -X POST "$BASE/query" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-API-Key: $KEY" \
  -d '{"subject":"Zeus","relation":"domain"}'
# Known → ACCEPTED + value · Unknown → ABSTAINED / empty</pre>
      </div>
      <div class="codebox" data-panel="chain" hidden>
        <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="chain">Copy</button>
        <pre id="code-chain">curl -sS -X POST "$BASE/chain" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-API-Key: $KEY" \
  -d '{"start":"Zeus","relations":["parent_of","domain"]}'
# Body: start + relations[] · returns value, status, path</pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="bench">
    <h2>Invent rate — measured on the real bench</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      The honest-abstention harness learns known facts, then asks unknowns.
      Invent rate is how often the system returns a non-empty answer when it should abstain.
      We publish the number after a clean host run of the real bench — not before.
    </p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <span class="badge badge-soon">PUBLISHING SOON</span>
        <h3>Invent rate</h3>
        <p>Measured on the real bench (<code>scripts/ops/bench_vs_llm.py</code> / Titanos learn+ask).
          The public figure lands here once the upstream harness runs clean on a host and the report is reviewed.</p>
        <p class="micro" style="margin-top:12px">
          What it measures: exact match on stored facts, and invent rate on unknowns
          (empty / ABSTAINED expected). LLM baseline optional via <code>BENCH_LLM_URL</code>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="badge">WHY IT MATTERS</span>
        <h3>Stores, derives, abstains</h3>
        <p>On structured truth, approximating models can invent under pressure.
          This system’s claim is operational: keep exact facts, derive from them, refuse the rest —
          and get stronger as hubs fill.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="badge badge-soon">ALSO PENDING</span>
        <h3>Composition &amp; assertion</h3>
        <p>Compositional and invention-without-hallucination tables stay empty until host runs populate them.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt" id="roadmap">
    <div class="inner">
      <h2>Next <span class="pending">ROADMAP · NOT SHIPPED</span></h2>
      <p class="sub">Labeled clearly so buyers do not confuse ambition with the deliverable.</p>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-soon">NEXT</span>
          <h3>Persona on the hub</h3>
          <p>Deeper persona packs living under <code>user:</code> with tone that never overrides store rows.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-soon">NEXT</span>
          <h3>Kin cycle on the hub</h3>
          <p>Iris → Metis → Hermes / eat cycle scoped to hub basins (routes exist; hub-native UX next).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-soon">NEXT</span>
          <h3>Speculative mouth behind the gate</h3>
          <p>Language only from stored rows — mouth renders; gate still owns truth.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-soon">NEXT</span>
          <h3>More hubs · more facts</h3>
          <p>Capability grows with seeded basins and verified facts — not with model size theatre.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

