  <section id="faq" class="faq">
    <h2>FAQ</h2>
    <details open>
      <summary>What does Resileos do?</summary>
      <p>It remembers exact facts you teach it, derives from those facts, and abstains when it does not know.
        Capability grows as your hubs fill. It does not invent answers to fill the gap.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need Docker to try it?</summary>
      <p>No. Visitors use Studio + a free key. Docker and compose are for developers self-hosting — see the GitHub HOSTING docs.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What is float32 about?</summary>
      <p>The classical core defaults to float32 state (<code>RESILEOS_STATE_DTYPE</code> unset) so storage and RAM stay practical on normal hardware. float64 is opt-in.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Where is the free-key API?</summary>
      <p>Issued by this site’s billing service (<code>POST /api/free-key</code>). The main Resileos API still authenticates with hashed keys in <code>configs/api_keys.json</code> — point both at the same file when you deploy.</p>
    </details>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <div>
